      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:51:6",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) إِنَّ بَعْضَ النَّاسِ يَقُولُ جَرِّدِ الْحَجَّ وَ بَعْضَ النَّاسِ يَقُولُ اقْرُنْ وَ سُقْ وَ بَعْضَ النَّاسِ يَقُولُ تَمَتَّعْ بِالْعُمْرَةِ إِلَى الْحَجِّ فَقَالَ لَوْ حَجَجْتُ أَلْفَ عَامٍ لَمْ أَقْرُنْهَا إِلَّا مُتَمَتِّعاً ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ali Bin Al Hakam, and Ibn Abu Najran, from Safwan Al Jammal who said, ",
          "‘I said to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, ‘Some of the people are saying, ‘The Hajj is performed exclusively’, and some of the people are saying, ‘Pair it (with Umra) and usher (the sacrificial animal)’, and some of the people are saying, ‘Perform <span class=\"iTxt\">Tamatto</span> with the Umra to the Hajj’. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘If I<sup>asws</sup> were to perform Hajj for a thousand years, I<sup>asws</sup> would not be pairing it except with the <span class=\"iTxt\">Tamatto </span>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ‘Isma‘il ibn Marrar from Yunus from Mu‘awiyah who has said the following: “Abu `Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘One who performs al-Hajj should take advantage (al- Mut‘ah); we do not compromise with the book of Allah, most Majestic, most Glorious, and the Sunnah of His Holy prophet, O Allah, grant compensation to Muhammad and his family worthy of their services to Your cause.”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
